<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'

import CardRect from './lib/CardRect.abide'
import cardRect from './lib/CardRect.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import LoadMore from './lib/LoadMore.abide'
import loadMore from './lib/LoadMore.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import SizeToPanel from './lib/SizeToPanel.abide'
import sizeToPanel from './lib/SizeToPanel.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/abide-files/by-name',
        '/helpers/popover',
        '/components/chart',
        '/reactive/reactive',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/observe.test.ts',
            from: ["test('a delivery writes the value, and nothing before it does"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/observe.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('given no target, host is spread and each field is a value of its own",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/observe.test.ts',
            from: ["test('fifty observed elements share one observer of each kind"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/reports/lib/TrendOnceSeen.test.ts',
            from: ["test('the trend is drawn when first scrolled to"],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Size a chart to its panel">
        <p>Call it with nothing and spread its <code>host</code> on the element, then read
            <code>width</code> and <code>height</code> by name. The browser writes them after
            each layout, and until the first one they are <code>undefined</code>.</p>
        <Example code={sizeToPanel}><SizeToPanel /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Read the older activity when the end of the feed scrolls into view">
        <p>Hand a part a function and it is called with each reading instead.
            <code>observe.visible</code> reads whether the element is in the viewport, or inside
            the element <code>in</code> names.</p>
        <Example code={loadMore}><LoadMore /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Draw the pipeline trend the first time the report scrolls down to the chart">
        <p>Hand a part a reactive value and it writes there, holding what you gave it until
            the first reading. Pass <code>once: true</code> and the first <code>true</code> is the
            last thing written. The element stops being observed, so what the value gates mounts once and
            stays mounted when it scrolls away again.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import { observe, reactive } from '@abide/abide'

            import PipelineTrend from './PipelineTrend.abide'

            let seen = reactive(false)
            </script>

            <section class="min-h-60" {...observe.visible(seen, { once: true })}>
                {#if seen}<PipelineTrend />{/if}
            </section>
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Measure the size and the position of one card">
        <p>Spread two parts and each measures the element. <code>observe.rect</code>
            reads the rectangle <code>getBoundingClientRect</code> reports, read again at most
            once a frame as the page scrolls or the card moves.</p>
        <Example code={cardRect}><CardRect /></Example>
    </Section>
</Doc>
